🚽 Test case: #193 -- a by-value struct member reached through a `chungus`
🚽 (union) works as a struct argument (`show(s.pt)`) exactly as for a
🚽 `gang`, since resolve_by_value_struct_source() treats both uniformly
🚽 (PR #253 review, finding 3 -- the union case the comments advertised
🚽 but the suite didn't cover).
gang Point {
    rizz x;
    rizz y;
};
chungus Shape {
    gang Point pt;
    rizz raw;
};

skibidi show(gang Point p) {
    yapping("%d %d", p.x, p.y);
}

skibidi main {
    chungus Shape s;
    s.pt.x = 3;
    s.pt.y = 4;
    show(s.pt);
}
